      "quantity": 1,
      "description": "<p>These blades come in a variety of shapes and styles, but they are typically 2 feet long.</p>",
      "level": 0,
      "price": "9 sp",
      "traits": [
        "agile",
        "finesse",
        "versatile-s"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Disguise Kit",
      "quantity": 1,
      "description": "<p>This small wooden box contains cosmetics, false facial hair, spirit gum, and a few simple wigs. You usually need a disguise kit to set up a disguise in order to Impersonate someone using the Deception skill. If you've crafted a large number of disguises, you can replenish your cosmetics supply with replacement cosmetics suitable for the type of your disguise kit. You can draw and replace a worn disguise kit as part of the action that uses it.</p>",
      "level": 0,
      "price": "2 gp",
      "traits": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Thieves' Toolkit",
      "quantity": 1,
      "description": "<p>You need a thieves' toolkit to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Pick a Lock]{Pick Locks} or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Disable a Device]{Disable Devices} (of some types) using the Thievery skill.</p>\n<p>If your thieves' toolkit is broken, you can repair it by replacing the lock picks with @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.Thieves' Toolkit (Replacement Picks)]{Replacement Picks} appropriate to your toolkit; this doesn't require using the Repair action. If you wear your thieves' toolkit, you can draw and replace it as part of the action that uses it.</p>",
      "level": 0,
      "price": "3 gp",
      "traits": []
    }
  ],
  "generalAbilities": [
    {
      "name": "Fence's Eye",
      "actions": null,
      "traits": [],
      "description": "<p>Fences can use underworld-lore|traits:action:identify-magic to identify an item's value and Identify Magic on an item. They gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Underworld Lore checks when doing so, and to all Underworld Lore checks related to stolen items.</p>",
      "collapsed": false
    }
